1
00:00:01,541 --> 00:00:05,666
Part Three: Side Effects of 
Pain Medications and Conclusion

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,125
Different pain treatments
can have different side effects.

3
00:00:11,291 --> 00:00:15,375
For example, Gabapentin
can cause sleepiness or nausea,

4
00:00:15,583 --> 00:00:19,833
so we recommend taking the medication
at night before bedtime.

5
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:23,375
We can change the dosing so
there is a good balance of effectiveness

6
00:00:23,375 --> 00:00:27,541
in treating your nerve pain
and minimizing side effects.

7
00:00:27,708 --> 00:00:30,166
Opioids can cause constipation.

8
00:00:30,291 --> 00:00:33,666
For this,
we start everyone on a stool softener

9
00:00:33,666 --> 00:00:36,500
like Docusate also known as Colace.

10
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:39,291
When they start to take the opioid medication.

11
00:00:39,291 --> 00:00:44,000
Colace works by increasing the amount 
of water the stool absorbs from the gut,

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,375
making the stool
softer and easier to pass.

13
00:00:47,791 --> 00:00:52,875
You can often see relief in 1 to 3 days
when starting this medication.

14
00:00:53,041 --> 00:00:55,500
If needed, we can add other medicines

15
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:58,500
like Miralax or Senna to help.

16
00:00:58,625 --> 00:01:02,458
Miralax also increases
the water content in your stool

17
00:01:02,458 --> 00:01:05,750
making it easier to pass to ease
bowel movements.

18
00:01:05,916 --> 00:01:09,416
Senna on the other hand, works
by increasing the activity

19
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:12,458
of your intestines,
stimulating the muscles that line

20
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:17,666
the gut to help push stool along the bowel
and prompt a bowel movement.

21
00:01:18,666 --> 00:01:21,583
Opioid Overdose Symptoms and Safety

22
00:01:21,875 --> 00:01:25,958
It is important to be aware
of the symptoms of an opioid overdose,

23
00:01:25,958 --> 00:01:31,000
which can include drowsiness,
extreme sleepiness, and trouble breathing.

24
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,375
We give everyone
a nasal spray called naloxone

25
00:01:34,375 --> 00:01:37,583
to use in an emergency
in case of an overdose.

26
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,208
Remember, don't operate heavy machinery
or do anything dangerous

27
00:01:42,208 --> 00:01:44,791
after taking the opioid medication.

28
00:01:44,791 --> 00:01:48,875
And please have someone drive you to
and from radiation treatments.

29
00:01:49,625 --> 00:01:50,958
We're here for you.

30
00:01:50,958 --> 00:01:53,541
Going through radiotherapy can be tough,

31
00:01:53,541 --> 00:01:57,166
but remember
we are here to help you manage your pain.

32
00:01:58,291 --> 00:02:00,708
Don't
be afraid to tell us how you're feeling,

33
00:02:00,708 --> 00:02:04,416
and we'll work together
to make you as comfortable as possible.

34
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:07,125
Please reach out to your doctors or nurses

35
00:02:07,125 --> 00:02:09,750
with any questions
you may have along the way.

36
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:11,666
Thank you for watching.
